cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this study's data, engine, or findings, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Misconfigured by Default: Kubernetes Configuration Practices in the Wild, and an Audit of the Tools That Check Them"
authors:
  - family-names: Mallya
    given-names: Girish
repository-code: "https://github.com/mallyagirish/k8s-misconfig-study"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Replication package and checker for an empirical study of Kubernetes
  configuration practices across 16,243 YAML documents (151 rendered Helm
  charts and 60 GitHub repositories): a 25-rule analysis engine, per-rule
  precision validated on a 457-finding author-verified sample, and a
  comparative audit of kube-linter, kubeaudit, Polaris, and Checkov on
  identical input.
